{"currentVersion":12,"id":11,"name":"AssetManagementDataStandard_RouteName","type":"Table","serviceItemId":"f955c118272b462e9ce757405890b87f","cacheMaxAge":30,"displayField":"","description":"&lt;div style=\"text-align:Left;\"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;The Asset Management Data Standard (AMDS) Network Model Route Names dataset contains the Route Naming as part of the base network model data for New Zealand, sourced from various Road Controlling Authority (RCA) Asset Management Systems, Land Information New Zealand (LINZ) and KiwiRail.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;This is related to the AMDS Network Model (Network Element) Segment table as a many to many (M:M). This allows for multi names to be recorded against any given centreline segment. Names could include but not limited to: Route Names, Authorised Names, Operational Names, or Alternative Names.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;The Route names provides Full and Abbreviated Names which are generated using a specific naming conventions defined by the Road Name Group, which is evaluated as an expression of its parts, such as:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;- An expression for a Route Name could be: Route Number + Route Alpha + (Body2)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;- An expression for an Authorised Name could be: Prefix + Body + Type + Suffix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;It is expected that Names may contain macrons. A macron is type of special character used for some languages. In the Māori language, a macron is a line that appears over Māori vowels, such as a, e, i, o, u. Example: ā, Ā, ē, Ē, ī, Ī, ō, Ō, ū, Ū.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Non-Spatial (aspatial) data is to be provided in UTF-8 format. To support customers of the AMDS Network Model datasets and enable backwards compatibility, additional fields are provided in this dataset that will contain ASCII format data.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=\"margin:0;\